{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0CJ2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[rr]_f \\ar[rd] & & \\mathcal{Y} \\ar[ld] \\\\\n& \\mathcal{Z}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-lci-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7cf27cdb094b82a1ae78d64d9c495549d94274e71b1166b722aad796e584a769", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7e000ae7af24706a8187264390179ddb667be18c31f2adaf70080557055f5fea", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a commutative diagram of morphisms of algebraic stacks.\nAssume <MATH_0002> is smooth and\n<MATH_0003> is a local complete intersection morphism.\nThen <MATH_0004> is a\nlocal complete intersection morphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e3c362a8c37b70a2c537f2fb18c7a3fd4140f424a55456d5300b0bf3594f6781", "unit_id": "tag:0CJ6:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0CJ2", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$W$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to W \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to W$", "MATH_0008": "$V \\to W$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-lci-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8107a1d1fe5b8f21fda29dd32be3faa4ab9bf255076b62d7a7c603b4e4a934ca", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d34822b4e20528dd9db6c32c043f745bc40371a5e0b2e7700e277450987250ce", "source_text": "Choose a scheme <MATH_0001> and a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0002>.\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0003> and a surjective smooth morphism\n<MATH_0004>.\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0005> and a surjective smooth morphism\n<MATH_0006>.\nThen <MATH_0007> is a local complete intersection morphism of schemes and\n<MATH_0008> is a smooth morphism of schemes. By the result for schemes\n(More on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>)\nwe conclude that <MATH_0009> is a local complete intersection morphism.\nBy definition this means that <MATH_0010> is a local complete intersection morphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bd0fb74bc08528cc731e8ad2f62ae9ef43aa2b41b770540b9ff774c264f278ea", "unit_id": "tag:0CJ6:proof"}
